      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bellamy’s Mill, built around 1850 on Fishing Creek, operated as a spinning mill and helped fuel Whitakers’ early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofwhitakers.org/who_we_are/index.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Porter Houses and Armstrong Kitchen, a historic complex, was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2002.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitakers%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Whitakers straddles Edgecombe and Nash Counties, making it the northernmost town in both counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
